riodic-support","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The evidence mapping records a Lean proof of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-eventually-periodic-support"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-eventually-periodic-support"],"id":"long.thm-eventually-periodic-support","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 5.6 (Eventually periodic support)","locator":"Long record Theorem 5.6, p. 39, label thm:eventually-periodic-support","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For integers $b\\ge2$ and $m\\ge1$, if $A\\subseteq\\mathbb N$ is infinite and its membership is $m$-periodic from some threshold $N_0$ on (i.e. $n+m \\in A \\Leftrightarrow n \\in A$ for all $n \\ge N_0$), then $\\sum_{a\\in A,\\ a\\ge1}(b^a-1)^{-1}$ is irrational, by transferring irrationality across the finite symmetric difference from the shifted purely periodic set $A_{\\mathrm{pure}} := \\{n : n + m N_0 \\in\nA\\}$. **Hypotheses:** $b \\ge 2$, $m \\ge 1$, $N_0 \\in \\mathbb{N}$, eventual $m$-periodicity from $N_0$, $A$ infinite.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-eventually-periodic-support","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-eventually-periodic-support","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.thm-eventually-periodic-support%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSupportSeries_eventuallyPeriodic%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.thm-eventually-periodic-support%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSupportSeries_eventuallyPeriodic%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1